        <description>&lt;img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1621166856483-1725976c4e21?ixid=M3w0NjAwMjJ8MHwxfHJhbmRvbXx8fHx8fHx8fDE3NzY0OTk0NDV8&amp;ixlib=rb-4.1.0" alt="Featured image of post android-reverse-engineering-skill" /&gt;&lt;h1 id=&#34;simoneavogadroandroid-reverse-engineering-skill&#34;&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/SimoneAvogadro/android-reverse-engineering-skill&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;SimoneAvogadro/android-reverse-engineering-skill&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 id=&#34;android-reverse-engineering--api-extraction--claude-code-skill&#34;&gt;Android Reverse Engineering &amp;amp; API Extraction — Claude Code skill
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;A Claude Code skill that decompiles Android APK/XAPK/JAR/AAR files and &lt;strong&gt;extracts the HTTP APIs&lt;/strong&gt; used by the app — Retrofit endpoints, OkHttp calls, hardcoded URLs, authentication patterns — so you can document and reproduce them without the original source code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-it-does&#34;&gt;What it does
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decompiles&lt;/strong&gt; APK, XAPK, JAR, and AAR files using jadx and Fernflower/Vineflower (single engine or side-by-side comparison)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extracts and documents APIs&lt;/strong&gt;: Retrofit endpoints, OkHttp calls, hardcoded URLs, auth headers and tokens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Traces call flows&lt;/strong&gt; from Activities/Fragments through ViewModels and repositories down to HTTP calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyzes&lt;/strong&gt; app structure: manifest, packages, architecture patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Handles obfuscated code&lt;/strong&gt;: strategies for navigating ProGuard/R8 output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;requirements&#34;&gt;Requirements
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Java JDK 17+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/skylot/jadx&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;jadx&lt;/a&gt; (CLI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional (recommended):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/Vineflower/vineflower&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Vineflower&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/JetBrains/fernflower&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Fernflower&lt;/a&gt; — better output on complex Java code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/pxb1988/dex2jar&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;dex2jar&lt;/a&gt; — needed to use Fernflower on APK/DEX files&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;code&gt;plugins/android-reverse-engineering/skills/android-reverse-engineering/references/setup-guide.md&lt;/code&gt; for detailed installation instructions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;installation&#34;&gt;Installation
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;from-github-recommended&#34;&gt;From GitHub (recommended)
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Inside Claude Code, run:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;/plugin marketplace add SimoneAvogadro/android-reverse-engineering-skill
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;/plugin install android-reverse-engineering@android-reverse-engineering-skill
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The skill will be permanently available in all future sessions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;from-a-local-clone&#34;&gt;From a local clone
